WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.920
A single starlink satellite held its orbit to within 44 meters for three months while fighting atmosphere drag at 460 kilometers. This is SpaceX Daily, episode 128. Keeptrack.space followed the V2MO bus, this generation of starlink satellite, across 88.7 days at a perigee of 460.6 kilometers and an apogee of 477.6. Its B-star drag coefficient, the tracking term for how hard the air is hitting it, sat at 8.3 times

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:35.940
10 to the minus 4, with a mean motion derivative of 2.8 times 10 to the minus 4 revolutions per

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:41.320
day squared. Those figures would normally bleed altitude on an unpowered object, yet the

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:47.960
spacecraft finished 6,281 revolutions on active electric propulsion, meaning low thrust engines,

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:54.780
with 45 kg of propellant aboard. 29 m solar arrays add drag area, and the vehicle

00:00:54.780 --> 00:01:02.160
launched August 28th, 2025 from Kennedy Space Center pad 39A on Starling Group 10. Launch

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:10.240
mass was 575 kilograms against a dry mass of 530 on a body 4.1 meters long. Mean motion

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:18.610
ran 15.344 revolutions per day with a 93.8 minute period, and across 151 element sets the

00:01:18.610 --> 00:01:28.770
semi-major axis, the orbit's long radius shifted only from 6,847.26 kilometers to 6,847.22,

00:01:29.390 --> 00:01:31.910
staying inside a 236 meter band.

00:01:32.470 --> 00:01:39.110
The Federal Communications Commission, or FCC, approved a 15,000 satellite mobile non-geostationary

00:01:39.110 --> 00:01:45.410
system for Starlink mobile service to ordinary handsets, according to adhoc-news.de.

00:01:45.410 --> 00:01:51.230
SpaceX also acquired up to 14 megahertz of paired 800 megahertz spectrum from grain

00:01:51.230 --> 00:01:54.570
management, and the clearance arrived on October 6th.

00:01:54.930 --> 00:01:59.110
The license lets the existing constellation beam cellular service straight to compatible

00:01:59.110 --> 00:02:03.750
phones, and modest buying lifted shares 1.4% on that session.

00:02:04.430 --> 00:02:09.070
Elon Musk said SpaceX would have to offer lower prices to succeed in the Indian market.

00:02:09.610 --> 00:02:12.030
Market Screener reported on October 12th.

00:02:12.030 --> 00:02:16.550
The comment follows ongoing regulatory talks on satellite broadband entry.

00:02:16.930 --> 00:02:21.550
He named no specific price target, and the requirement ties to competitive positioning

00:02:21.550 --> 00:02:23.490
against existing Indian operators.

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:30.270
Crew Dragon Freedom splashed down in the Pacific off Los Angeles after 237 days on the International

00:02:30.270 --> 00:02:32.250
Space Station, or ISS.

00:02:33.090 --> 00:02:38.610
NASA and SpaceX now target an October 13th launch for the 35th commercial resupply mission,

00:02:38.610 --> 00:02:41.870
carrying more than 6,300 pounds of cargo.

00:02:42.470 --> 00:02:49.570
Docking is penciled in for October 15th, adhawk-news.d reports, and the crew 12 rotation once

00:02:49.570 --> 00:02:53.570
counted as a technological milestone, but now registers as routine.

00:02:54.210 --> 00:02:57.970
Turn around at this cadence-freeze operational capacity for other programs.

00:02:58.690 --> 00:03:03.350
Grok is now available inside Tesla Cyber Cab Rides, Musk posted on X.

00:03:03.350 --> 00:03:09.290
Riders sign in once, and the bot stays available across future trips, then logs out automatically

00:03:09.290 --> 00:03:12.190
the moment of passenger exits to preserve privacy.

00:03:12.650 --> 00:03:17.750
He tested it by adding laundry detergent to an Amazon cart during a ride, and the integration

00:03:17.750 --> 00:03:21.250
works on all future cybercab trips after that initial sign-in.

00:03:21.750 --> 00:03:26.650
Musk also posted a photo of a stainless steel cyber truck parked beside Starship at the

00:03:26.650 --> 00:03:27.210
launch site.

00:03:27.730 --> 00:03:32.630
Both structures use the same stainless steel alloy, sharing material properties that support

00:03:32.630 --> 00:03:34.330
durability in harsh environments.

00:03:34.890 --> 00:03:40.570
Ship 40, the Starship Upper Stage, returned to Texas after 75 days at sea following its

00:03:40.570 --> 00:03:46.070
ocean test campaign, a tracker account from techinsider.org that the company has not confirmed.

00:03:46.630 --> 00:03:51.750
The Upper Stage completed its return transport and now sits at the Starbase facility after

00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:55.670
the extended seetime-tested recovery hardware under real-world conditions.

00:03:56.490 --> 00:04:01.770
KSBY has a Falcon 9 launch from Vandenberg Space Force Base, targeted from Monday evening.

00:04:01.770 --> 00:04:07.370
A Starlink mission is also listed from Monday afternoon from the same California site, Ed

00:04:07.370 --> 00:04:10.790
Hot Notes, which would put consecutive activity on that range.

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:17.470
Musk shared a 240p video of Shuttle Columbia launching toward Hubble in 2002, and noted

00:04:17.470 --> 00:04:19.910
that public viewing of launches remains popular.

00:04:20.410 --> 00:04:24.910
The clip shows the shuttle lighting up the Florida sky during Ascent, and observers said

00:04:24.910 --> 00:04:28.370
even the low-resolution footage still captures why crowds show up.

00:04:28.370 --> 00:04:33.190
One thing worth watching is that Starlink still has to complete security assessments and

00:04:33.190 --> 00:04:38.310
receive spectrum assignments in India before service can begin, even if pricing is adjusted.

00:04:38.890 --> 00:04:43.630
Three other licensed operators already hold Indian approvals and could move faster on rollout,

00:04:43.930 --> 00:04:44.910
market screener reports.

00:04:45.550 --> 00:04:50.890
The regulatory path remains the binding constraint on market entry, and without those clearances,

00:04:51.130 --> 00:04:54.230
even lower prices cannot translate into operational service.

00:04:54.230 --> 00:05:00.790
On the AI front, Musk said XAI plans to use Nvidia hardware exclusively for its data centers,

00:05:01.170 --> 00:05:04.610
and Colossus 2 could more than double its chip count by December,

00:05:05.170 --> 00:05:11.230
strat news global reports. $40 billion in financing talks with banks and PIMCO remain ongoing

00:05:11.230 --> 00:05:15.670
to support the purchases, with Apollo expected to lead distribution of the debt.

00:05:16.230 --> 00:05:21.890
The talks involve roughly $10 billion in bank loans and $30 billion in investment grade bonds.

00:05:21.890 --> 00:05:27.030
ones. Pull the engineering angle apart and drag is just density time speed squared times

00:05:27.030 --> 00:05:32.610
area. Stealing kinetic energy the thrusters have to put back. Orbital speed in this band

00:05:32.610 --> 00:05:38.670
is on the order of 7.6 kilometers per second, so even 10 to the power of minus 11 kilograms

00:05:38.670 --> 00:05:44.170
per cubic meter of residual air packs a punch because force scales with velocity squared.

00:05:44.170 --> 00:05:51.150
Earth's mean radius is about 6,371 kilometers, which is why a semi-major axis near

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:55.810
6,800 kilometers still flies through the thermosphere rather than through vacuum.

00:05:56.490 --> 00:05:58.150
Density there is not a constant.

00:05:58.770 --> 00:06:03.710
Solar extreme ultraviolet and geomagnetic storms can swing it by a factor of 10 or more,

00:06:04.170 --> 00:06:07.990
which is why a quiet week and a storm week do not cost the same propellant.

00:06:08.590 --> 00:06:13.910
The thermospheric scale height is on the order of 60 kilometers, so a small drop in altitude

00:06:13.910 --> 00:06:18.570
raises drag sharply, and that is the ratchet an unpowered object cannot reverse.

00:06:19.230 --> 00:06:23.590
Stations flying near 400 kilometers replace lost energy with chemical burns

00:06:23.590 --> 00:06:28.030
measured in kilonutons for seconds. A small satellite does the same job with

00:06:28.030 --> 00:06:32.730
millenuton-class electric thrust stretched over months. A typical hall-effect

00:06:32.730 --> 00:06:37.370
thruster, a solar-powered engine that accelerates ions from a noble gas feed,

00:06:37.870 --> 00:06:43.550
delivers on the order of 1,500 to 2,000 seconds of specific impulse, which is how

00:06:43.550 --> 00:06:46.170
How many seconds of thrust do you get per unit of propellant?

00:06:46.590 --> 00:06:50.050
Against 9.81 meters per second squared of standard gravity.

00:06:50.650 --> 00:06:56.210
Chemical monoperpellant sits near a 300 seconds, so electric propulsion is roughly 6 times

00:06:56.210 --> 00:07:01.290
stingier with mass for the same delta V. The change in velocity the orbit actually needs.

00:07:01.990 --> 00:07:06.430
Back of envelope, that class of engine can buy more than a kilometer per second of total

00:07:06.430 --> 00:07:11.630
delta V from a small consumable load, which is why short burns can cancel drag instead

00:07:11.630 --> 00:07:17.430
of fighting it continuously. The thrusters therefore run at a very low duty cycle. The fraction

00:07:17.430 --> 00:07:22.270
of time they are actually firing, lighting only when a density spike walks the orbit out of

00:07:22.270 --> 00:07:27.270
tolerance. Those same arrays have to make extra kilowatts for inter-satellite laser links,

00:07:27.690 --> 00:07:34.170
which cut ground station dependence. And the solar constant at Earth is roughly 1,360 watts per

00:07:34.170 --> 00:07:40.370
square meter before cell efficiency, pointing cosine and eclipse. That is the trade. More area

00:07:40.370 --> 00:07:45.770
means more drag and more power, and the loop only closes if stationkeeping stays a thin slice

00:07:45.770 --> 00:07:52.130
of dry mass, so structure, radios, and lasers still fit. Magic wand, the consumable as raw

00:07:52.130 --> 00:07:57.230
noble gas and a few square meters of silicon, and the flown article still adds thrusters,

00:07:57.810 --> 00:08:03.470
deployable structure, pointing, and optical terminals. So the idiot index, how many times the

00:08:03.470 --> 00:08:10.350
finished article costs over those raw inputs, sits on the order of 10 to 50. The 53 degree operational

00:08:10.350 --> 00:08:14.950
shell is where this budget has to work for every vehicle in the plane, not for a single

00:08:14.950 --> 00:08:15.970
well-behaved bird.

00:08:16.490 --> 00:08:20.790
Over longer time scales, the same propulsion and power balance sets how many satellites

00:08:20.790 --> 00:08:23.250
can share an altitude band before propellant.

00:08:23.750 --> 00:08:25.710
Not the launch ticket becomes the limiter.

00:08:26.290 --> 00:08:31.790
A future V3 or V4 that grows the arrays further will need either higher specific impulse

00:08:31.790 --> 00:08:34.610
or a lower drag layout to hold the same stability.

00:08:35.190 --> 00:08:38.910
Because laser-link traffic and attitude control will eat the same tank.

00:08:38.910 --> 00:08:43.770
The current pairing already shows the electric propulsion and solar array loop can close

00:08:43.770 --> 00:08:49.310
at these altitudes, which is what lets thousands more V2MO class vehicles occupy the same

00:08:49.310 --> 00:08:49.670
shells.

00:08:50.270 --> 00:08:52.710
Across the tape, shares finished roughly flat.

00:08:53.210 --> 00:08:57.490
Before we go, weather and range constraints will determine final timing on the California

00:08:57.490 --> 00:09:00.770
